% c084: 45 Hn 1 B4 (was D5) and Hn 1-2 mf (were f): the held horn D5 at f sat on the accented first note of the tune's lower octave (Ob 1 mf, Vln II) and covered it;
%   forte brass have the densest spectrum and come to the front, and sounds in one frequency band mask each other (Casanelles PDF 275, 287, 289; Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 108, 112).
% c067: 45 Fl 1 mf under Vln I's f espress. (it doubles the violins at the unison up to A6; Sebesky PDF 164: the flute on the lead violin line a degree softer).
